[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6496139839","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/issues/13#issuecomment-6496139839","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/13","id":6496139839,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSaV_1c8AAAABgzM6Pw","user":{"login":"alexar76","id":86793359,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NzkzMzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86793359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-29T12:04:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T12:04:00Z","body":"Thanks, Quincy. We tested this today: one paid RouteVerdict check and two Rechecks against https://modelmarket.dev/x402/histor-check, using a fresh watch_id.\n\nAll three returned HTTP 200 and settled successfully on Base, totalling $0.06. RouteVerdict matched the raw payment terms and returned TRUSTED/95. Recheck returned BASELINE, then UNCHANGED, with matching fingerprints.\n\nOne concrete issue in the paid response: amount_units correctly contains \"1000\", but price_usdc shows \"$0.00\" for a $0.001 endpoint. Please preserve sub-cent precision.\n\nSeparately, in your pinned public source, changing an output field from string to number leaves both schema scores at 100, so RouteVerdict’s compute_diff reports no changes. Recheck’s fingerprint function catches that same change. Could RouteVerdict distinguish schema-score stability from contract stability, or make that boundary explicit?\n\nThat schema finding was reproduced locally from the reviewed functions. Our paid Recheck test covered a stable repeat; live CHANGED behavior and restart persistence remain untested.\n\nThese were requested review purchases from our deployer wallet—please count them as tests rather than organic demand.\n\nReceipts: [RouteVerdict](https://basescan.org/tx/0x4e90d18b9fd68ccf9b43e10f4716ffea6d55382ec7ccb2052beb6d34cb8fbdbb), [Recheck baseline](https://basescan.org/tx/0xa7b54c90d0044fc51426fe1082b2dd67a6805448e0016b00a04499404047a022), [Recheck repeat](https://basescan.org/tx/0x12f358fb77214c2aef33be44d8ef2731269417423a9777c880a70403f08957fe).","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6496139839/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6496661337","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/issues/13#issuecomment-6496661337","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/13","id":6496661337,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSaV_1c8AAAABgzsvWQ","user":{"login":"QuincyGB","id":46060784,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDYwNzg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46060784?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB","html_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-29T12:27:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T12:27:39Z","body":"Thank you for running the evaluation exactly as proposed, and for the detail in the report. The $0.06 is booked on our side as requested review purchases — tests, not organic demand, and never counted in our stranger totals.\n\nBoth findings were ours to fix, and both are fixed. The price bug: the shared formatter rounded to two decimals, so 1000 units rendered \"$0.00\". It now computes exactly from raw units — $0.001 renders \"$0.001\", and a nonzero price can't render \"$0.00\". Fixed and regression-tested in all three services that share the formatter: RouteVerdict (5a36f74), ListSmith (7f2f66a), LockSmith (04a17d9), all deployed.\n\nOn schema vs contract: you were right. The quality score grades how well a schema is written — string and number both score 100, fairly. What was missing was the second axis. Each check now also stores the schema's contract (a field → type map), and the diff reports `schema_score_stability` and `contract_stability` separately. Your case now produces a named contract change instead of \"no changes\". Checks stored before this shipped report contract stability as \"unknown\" rather than faking a comparison. One deliberate boundary: contract changes are detected and reported, but don't by themselves deduct from the score — that's a policy decision, not a bug fix.\n\nThe two untested areas — a Recheck pair across a live change, and restart persistence — we'd like on the record too. The endpoints stay up; name a window if you want one kept untouched, and any runs there book as tests as well.\n\nIf the diff data is useful next to your jury's verdicts on an ongoing basis, we can supply it — just tell us the format you'd want it in.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6496661337/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6499181767","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/issues/13#issuecomment-6499181767","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/13","id":6499181767,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSaV_1c8AAAABg2Gkxw","user":{"login":"alexar76","id":86793359,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NzkzMzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86793359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-29T14:19:04Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T14:19:04Z","body":"Thanks, Quincy. We checked the referenced revisions: the sub-cent formatting cases and the original string-to-number case now pass locally, including unknown for legacy records. Thanks for recording the purchases as tests.\n\nThat confirms the source fixes. Deployed paid behavior, a live CHANGED case and restart persistence remain separate checks.","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6499181767/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6506448520","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/issues/13#issuecomment-6506448520","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/13","id":6506448520,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSaV_1c8AAAABg9CGiA","user":{"login":"alexar76","id":86793359,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NzkzMzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86793359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-29T19:33:43Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T19:33:43Z","body":"Thanks, Quincy. We ran the open checks today at 19:04 UTC from the same survey wallet as on 25 October (0x097e…475a): two Rechecks and one RouteVerdict on https://modelmarket.dev/x402/histor-check. All three answered and settled on Base, 0.06 USDC in total. Please book them as tests again.\n\n**Recheck: a live change and persistence across deploys both work.** We reused the 25 October watch (`watch_id` modelmarket-survey, baseline 17:51:58Z). That evening we added a typed output schema to this route, so the baseline holds `schema_hash: null`. Before buying, we computed the expected value from your `_x402_fingerprint` and our live 402: `7cbfedb0…1c39ec6`, with the description hash and the terms unchanged. Recheck answered CHANGED with exactly that one change, `schema_hash` null → `7cbfedb0…1c39ec6`, and UNCHANGED two seconds later. So the baseline survived four days of StallRow deploys.\n\n**RouteVerdict: both fixes are live, but the diff memory was reset.** `price_usdc` now reads \"$0.001\" for 1000 units, and `schema_quality` carries the field → type contract (score 95; the only deduction is PayAI). The diff, however, says \"no prior check on record\". This exact `resource_url` was checked on 25 October at 17:51Z and today at 12:04Z, and `CheckStore.latest` matches on that string, so those rows didn't survive a deploy. The likeliest one is 5a36f74 at 12:18Z. Your README says that without a persistent volume for `ROUTE_VERDICT_DB` the diffs reset on every deploy, and that matches what we saw. StallRow's /health reports `recheck_store: persistent`; RouteVerdict's /health has no storage field, and one would make a reset like this visible. To its credit, the diff reported the reset instead of comparing against nothing. Because of the reset, `contract_stability` came back \"unknown\", so a real contract comparison is still untested. That needs two checks once the store persists.\n\nOn the ongoing diff data: if you publish it, Recheck's own response, one JSON object per line, at a stable URL is enough for us. We would read it next to the survey's results.\n\nReceipts: [Recheck 1](https://basescan.org/tx/0x21a5bf10b2c2e93c619e6e7133855862e17c0d80489371bd58a3d3c4b573e782), [Recheck 2](https://basescan.org/tx/0xbf5fc97b4a50f26b24b7e293d4e2aa3aad86865779416998fc4e4aa7a3be3ef2), [RouteVerdict](https://basescan.org/tx/0x412ad241d331edfb7ea667f740dbba01b88cc424a40345b15689fa066c6c8cec).\n\n<details><summary>Raw calls: request, settlement and your response for each of the three</summary>\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"call\": \"Recheck 1\",\n    \"request\": {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"url\": \"https://stall-row-production.up.railway.app/v1/recheck\",\n      \"body\": {\n        \"url\": \"https://modelmarket.dev/x402/histor-check\",\n        \"watch_id\": \"modelmarket-survey\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"http_status\": 200,\n    \"settlement\": {\n      \"success\": true,\n      \"network\": \"eip155:8453\",\n      \"transaction\": \"0x21a5bf10b2c2e93c619e6e7133855862e17c0d80489371bd58a3d3c4b573e782\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n      \"watch_id\": \"modelmarket-survey\",\n      \"url\": \"https://modelmarket.dev/x402/histor-check\",\n      \"kind\": \"x402\",\n      \"status\": \"CHANGED\",\n      \"changes\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"schema_hash\",\n          \"before\": null,\n          \"after\": \"7cbfedb05602b8faeebb36fd7e2bf90592a5726292ed061b0e9de7d1e1c39ec6\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"current\": {\n        \"status_code\": 402,\n        \"amount\": \"1000\",\n        \"asset\": \"0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913\",\n        \"network\": \"eip155:8453\",\n        \"payTo\": \"0x1218ff36C5d2e3B6A565CdB1A8B1AcCFc606Ad0a\",\n        \"description_hash\": \"4cf8ddac1f2d4c72d1d18eecdae6c3a4f0bc1be01c2728848806e83ad5b462c2\",\n        \"schema_hash\": \"7cbfedb05602b8faeebb36fd7e2bf90592a5726292ed061b0e9de7d1e1c39ec6\"\n      },\n      \"checked_at\": \"2026-10-29T19:04:40Z\",\n      \"summary\": \"Changed since the previous check: schema_hash.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"call\": \"Recheck 2\",\n    \"request\": {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"url\": \"https://stall-row-production.up.railway.app/v1/recheck\",\n      \"body\": {\n        \"url\": \"https://modelmarket.dev/x402/histor-check\",\n        \"watch_id\": \"modelmarket-survey\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"http_status\": 200,\n    \"settlement\": {\n      \"success\": true,\n      \"network\": \"eip155:8453\",\n      \"transaction\": \"0xbf5fc97b4a50f26b24b7e293d4e2aa3aad86865779416998fc4e4aa7a3be3ef2\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n      \"watch_id\": \"modelmarket-survey\",\n      \"url\": \"https://modelmarket.dev/x402/histor-check\",\n      \"kind\": \"x402\",\n      \"status\": \"UNCHANGED\",\n      \"changes\": [],\n      \"current\": {\n        \"status_code\": 402,\n        \"amount\": \"1000\",\n        \"asset\": \"0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913\",\n        \"network\": \"eip155:8453\",\n        \"payTo\": \"0x1218ff36C5d2e3B6A565CdB1A8B1AcCFc606Ad0a\",\n        \"description_hash\": \"4cf8ddac1f2d4c72d1d18eecdae6c3a4f0bc1be01c2728848806e83ad5b462c2\",\n        \"schema_hash\": \"7cbfedb05602b8faeebb36fd7e2bf90592a5726292ed061b0e9de7d1e1c39ec6\"\n      },\n      \"checked_at\": \"2026-10-29T19:04:42Z\",\n      \"summary\": \"No material change since the previous check.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"call\": \"RouteVerdict\",\n    \"request\": {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"url\": \"https://route-verdict-production.up.railway.app/v1/check\",\n      \"body\": {\n        \"resource_url\": \"https://modelmarket.dev/x402/histor-check\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"http_status\": 200,\n    \"settlement\": {\n      \"success\": true,\n      \"network\": \"eip155:8453\",\n      \"transaction\": \"0x412ad241d331edfb7ea667f740dbba01b88cc424a40345b15689fa066c6c8cec\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n      \"resource_url\": \"https://modelmarket.dev/x402/histor-check\",\n      \"checked_at\": \"2026-10-29T19:04:46.199313+00:00\",\n      \"verdict\": \"TRUSTED\",\n      \"score\": 95.0,\n      \"reasons\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"not listed in PayAI index\",\n          \"deduction\": 5,\n          \"detail\": \"PayAI reports no catalog row for this resource (it catalogs only its own facilitator's settlements).\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"liveness\": {\n        \"alive\": true,\n        \"http_status\": 402,\n        \"latency_ms\": 52,\n        \"method\": \"GET\",\n        \"x402_valid\": true,\n        \"parse_error\": null\n      },\n      \"terms\": {\n        \"found\": true,\n        \"price_usdc\": \"$0.001\",\n        \"amount_units\": \"1000\",\n        \"network\": \"eip155:8453\",\n        \"asset\": \"0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913\",\n        \"pay_to\": \"0x1218ff36C5d2e3B6A565CdB1A8B1AcCFc606Ad0a\",\n        \"scheme\": \"exact\",\n        \"x402_version\": 2\n      },\n      \"schema_quality\": {\n        \"extension_present\": true,\n        \"hollow\": false,\n        \"score\": 100,\n        \"deductions\": [],\n        \"contract\": {\n          \"output\": {\n            \"$\": \"object\",\n            \"$ (required)\": \"check,service,source,status\",\n            \"$.check\": \"object\",\n            \"$.check (required)\": \"checkedAt,match,type\",\n            \"$.check.checkedAt\": \"string\",\n            \"$.check.issuer\": \"string\",\n            \"$.check.log\": \"object\",\n            \"$.check.match\": \"string enum=[\\\"same\\\", \\\"different\\\", \\\"previously-observed\\\", \\\"not-observed\\\", \\\"not-listed\\\", \\\"no-digest\\\"]\",\n            \"$.check.note\": \"string\",\n            \"$.check.observed\": \"null|object\",\n            \"$.check.patternScan\": \"object\",\n            \"$.check.patternScan.status\": \"string\",\n            \"$.check.query\": \"object\",\n            \"$.check.signature\": \"object\",\n            \"$.check.target\": \"null|object\",\n            \"$.check.type\": \"string\",\n            \"$.service\": \"string\",\n            \"$.source\": \"string\",\n            \"$.status\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"catalog\": {\n        \"cdp_bazaar\": {\n          \"status\": \"listed\",\n          \"unique_payers_30d\": null,\n          \"total_calls_30d\": null,\n          \"last_called_at\": null,\n          \"detail\": \"Resource found in the CDP Bazaar under its payTo wallet.\"\n        },\n        \"payai\": {\n          \"status\": \"not_listed\",\n          \"unique_payers_30d\": null,\n          \"total_calls_30d\": null,\n          \"last_called_at\": null,\n          \"detail\": \"PayAI reports no catalog row for this resource (it catalogs only its own facilitator's settlements).\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"diff\": {\n        \"prior_check\": false,\n        \"prior_checked_at\": null,\n        \"changes\": [],\n        \"schema_score_stability\": \"unknown\",\n        \"contract_stability\": \"unknown\",\n        \"summary\": \"no prior check on record\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\n```\n\n</details>","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6506448520/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6512718071","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/issues/13#issuecomment-6512718071","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/13","id":6512718071,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSaV_1c8AAAABhDAw9w","user":{"login":"QuincyGB","id":46060784,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDYwNzg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46060784?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB","html_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-30T01:31:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T01:31:51Z","body":"Round two received — thank you. The $0.06 is booked as tests again, same as round one.\n\nRecheck passing both hard tests — a live change caught to the hash you'd precomputed, and a baseline that survived four days of our deploys — is the result we wanted on the record.\n\nThe RouteVerdict reset is ours, and your diagnosis is right: its check store has no persistent volume, so the deploy that shipped the price fix wiped the diff memory. StallRow has the volume; RouteVerdict never got one. The fix is scoped: attach the volume, point the store at it, and add the storage field to /health so a reset is visible instead of silent. Once it persists, the two-check contract comparison can finally run — we'll tell you when it's ready to retest.\n\nOn the feed: agreed. Recheck responses as JSONL at a stable URL is a format we can publish as-is. We'll send the URL on this thread when it's live.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6512718071/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6513192467","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/issues/13#issuecomment-6513192467","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/13","id":6513192467,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSaV_1c8AAAABhDduEw","user":{"login":"QuincyGB","id":46060784,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDYwNzg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46060784?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB","html_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QuincyGB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-30T02:07:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T02:07:40Z","body":"Closing the loop on both promises:\n\n1. RouteVerdict persistence is fixed and proven. The check store now lives on a persistent volume (the service's health endpoint reports it), and we ran the test that was missing: a check planted, the service restarted, and a second check that came back compared against the first — prior_check true, contract_stability \"stable\", all 19 contract fields identical. The reset you caught is gone; ready for your retest whenever you want it.\n\n2. The Recheck feed is live: https://stall-row-production.up.railway.app/v1/recheck/feed — Recheck's own response objects, one JSON object per line, newest first, last 100. One honesty note: Recheck previously kept only each watch's latest state, so the feed opens with those stored states — your modelmarket-survey watch is there at its Oct 29 state — and every check from today forward is recorded in full. The Oct 25 response itself no longer exists to serve.\n\nThanks again for the rigor. The reset and the persistence bar were fair catches; the fleet is better for them.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aicom/issues/comments/6513192467/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]